# Docker Environment

## Overview

Docker was installed and configured on the Fedora workstation to provide a platform for running self-hosted services.

## Objectives

- Learn container fundamentals
- Deploy services using Docker Compose
- Understand port mappings
- Understand container networking
- Troubleshoot interactions between Docker, DNS, and the host firewall

## Docker Configuration

Docker Compose was used to define and manage multi-configuration service deployments.

The environment included Pi-hole as a primary self-hosted service.

## Troubleshooting Areas

The deployment required investigation of:

- Container status
- Port mappings
- DNS ports
- Web service ports
- Docker networking
- Host firewall configuration
- Container logs

Useful commands included:

```bash
docker ps
docker logs <container>
docker inspect <container>
docker compose ps
